{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"b0v0mixxd","tool_use_id":"toolu_01TP3mTqincsUuHVuEUfeyFi","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run2-repo/edde3eb1-2123-4a90-9f7c-b0009a064343/tasks/b0v0mixxd.output","summary":"Background command \"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_3\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nRefinement of the incumbent `terminal_streak_recency_pattern_rule` (tally span judged against a personal expected span, switching judged by closeness to a personal ideal switching rate, chunk variety and a rule-built penalty scaled by a personal pattern sensitivity, a shared penalty on the streak a sequence ends on, a personal left/right lean). The one change: people also notice a local stretch of strict alternation as a pattern in its own right — every four-flip stretch that zig-zags perfectly (HTHT or THTH) counts against a sequence's randomness, by a shared local-alternation penalty, even when its overall switching rate is the same as its partner's. Of two sequences with equal switch counts, people therefore pick the one whose switches are not bunched into an extended zig-zag, addressing the critique that among equal-switch pairs people choose the sequence with fewer strictly alternating four-flip windows more often than the incumbent predicts.\nEOF\necho local_zigzag_terminal_streak_pattern_rule > $D/model_name.txt\npython3 - << 'PY'\nsrc=open(\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/models/terminal_streak_recency_pattern_rule.py\").read()\ndoc_old=src[:src.index('import numpy')]\ndoc='''\"\"\"Local zig-zag penalty on the terminal-streak recency pattern-rule judgement.\n\nRefinement of `terminal_streak_recency_pattern_rule`: tally span judged against\na personal expected span, switching by closeness to a personal ideal switching\nrate, chunk variety and a rule-built penalty scaled by a personal pattern\nsensitivity, a shared penalty on the final streak, and a personal left/right\nlean. The one change: every four-flip window that strictly alternates (HTHT or\nTHTH) counts against a sequence's randomness (a shared local-alternation\npenalty), so among equal-switch pairs people pick the sequence whose switches\nare not bunched into an extended zig-zag.\n\"\"\"\n'''\nsrc=doc+src[len(doc_old):]\nsrc=src.replace('''    a = sequence_a.strip().upper()''','''    def zigzag_windows(seq):\n        # Number of four-flip windows that strictly alternate (HTHT / THTH).\n        return float(sum(\n            1 for i in range(len(seq) - 3)\n            if seq[i] != seq[i + 1] and seq[i + 1] != seq[i + 2] and seq[i + 2] != seq[i + 3]\n        ))\n\n    a = sequence_a.strip().upper()''')\nsrc=src.replace('''        \"log_len\":''','''        \"zig_diff\": zigzag_windows(a) - zigzag_windows(b),\n        \"log_len\":''')\nsrc=src.replace('''    log_len = pm.Data(\"log_len\"''','''    zig_diff = pm.Data(\"zig_diff\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    log_len = pm.Data(\"log_len\"''')\nsrc=src.replace('''    # Person-specific left/right''','''    # The change: shared penalty per strictly alternating four-flip window.\n    eta = pm.Normal(\"eta\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)\n\n    # Person-specific left/right''')\nsrc=src.replace('''        - tau * term_diff\n''','''        - tau * term_diff\n        - eta * zig_diff\n''')\nsrc=src.replace(\"    # The change: shared penalty per flip of the final run\",\"    # Shared penalty per flip of the final run\")\nopen(\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_3/candidate.py\",\"w\").write(src)\nPY\ngrep -n \"zig\\|eta\" $D/candidate.py\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run2/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelin